  "description": "SIKYET crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C92 H124 Fe2 N2 O30 Tb4. From the CIF bond table, Fe1 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Fe2 (Fe) has 6 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.199-3.588 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.58-106.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C92H124Fe2Tb4N2O30. Article name explicitly identifies I(II).",
